.TH MU2EDAQ-TOOLS-INFO 1 "2026-07-27" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq-tools-info \- report the config file the C++ DAQ tools would use
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq-tools-info
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq-tools-info
is the C++ counterpart to
.BR "mu2edaq-tools config" .
It prints the version of the
.B mu2edaq_cli_core
library it was linked against and the YAML config file a C++ tool started from
the current working directory would read, without starting anything else.
.PP
It is a diagnostic: use it when a C++ and a Python tool disagree about their
settings, to see which file each one actually picked up.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Report on
.I FILE
instead of searching the standard locations.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-paths
List every candidate path in search order, marking the one in use with
.BR * .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG
Config file to use when
.B \-\-config
is not given.
.SH FILES
The same search order as
.BR mu2edaq-tools (1),
minus the Python checkout entry:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG
./mu2edaq-commandline-tools.yaml
./config/mu2edaq-commandline-tools.yaml
~/.config/mu2edaq/commandline-tools.yaml
/etc/mu2edaq/commandline-tools.yaml
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
mu2edaq\-tools\-info \-\-paths
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-tools (1),
.BR mu2edaq_cli_core (3)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group.
